# --- Data, model weights, caches (never commit) ---
# Deliberately NOT `data/**` plus `!data/emotions_171.txt`. Git resolves an ignore
# file last-match-wins, so the negation re-includes the file; rsync's
# `--filter=':- .gitignore'` (used by scripts/sync_up.sh) resolves it
# FIRST-match-wins, so `data/**` won and the negation never fired -- the 171-word
# reference list silently never reached the pod. The two tools read the same file
# with opposite precedence, so any broad-exclude + negation pair here is a trap.
#
# Everything large that lands in data/ is covered by name below (hf_cache/,
# *.parquet, *.arrow, ...), so no directory-wide rule is needed and no negation
# has to override one.

# Hugging Face / torch caches
.cache/
hf_cache/
huggingface/
*.safetensors
*.parquet
*.arrow
*.bin
*.pt
*.pth
*.npy
*.npz

# --- Run outputs (activations, directions, eval artefacts) ---
outputs/**
!outputs/.gitkeep

# --- Notebooks / analysis scratch ---
.ipynb_checkpoints/
analysis/**/*.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.python-version

# --- Secrets ---
# r2.env is the real credentials file (R2 keys + HF_TOKEN); r2.env.example is the
# committed template. Note the negation must come after the ignore rule.
r2.env
!r2.env.example
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.runpod.local.env

# --- OS / editors ---
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

RUNPOD_WORKFLOW.md